lessons.body:
Authenticated Task Queries End
to End
Connect query functions to the real protected NestJS API

Phase 22 - TanStack Query
Volume 06 - Professional Frontend

Build an authenticated Task API client
TanStack Query does not perform HTTP requests itself. The query function calls TaskFlow's existing
authenticated API client. This keeps authentication, error parsing and HTTP semantics outside React
components.

export async function fetchTasks(query: TaskListQuery) {
const params = new URLSearchParams();
params.set("page", String(query.page));
params.set("pageSize", String(query.pageSize));
if (query.search) params.set("search", query.search);
if (query.status) params.set("status", query.status);
if (query.priority) params.set("priority", query.priority);

return authenticatedFetch<TaskPage>(
`/tasks?${params.toString()}`,
);
}

Client component reads cached server state
"use client";

export function TasksScreen({ query }: { query: TaskListQuery }) {
const result = useQuery(taskListOptions(query));

if (result.isPending) return <TaskListSkeleton />;
if (result.isError) return <TaskListError error={result.error} />;
if (result.data.data.length === 0) return <EmptyState />;

return (
<>
{result.isFetching ? <span>Refreshing...</span> : null}
<TaskTable tasks={result.data.data} />
</>
);
}

Keep the response shape typed
export type TaskPage = {
data: Task[];
meta: {
page: number;
pageSize: number;
totalItems: number;
totalPages: number;
hasPreviousPage: boolean;
hasNextPage: boolean;
};
};

One API client, many consumers

Server Components, TanStack Query hooks and form mutations should reuse the same transport contract where
practical. Do not create a new fetch wrapper inside every component.

Preserve the Phase 13 error contract
The API client should throw the structured ApiClientError created earlier, including status, stable error
code and requestId when available. TanStack Query stores that error as query state; it should not
flatten every failure into a generic fetch string.

Transport boundary checklist
Concern                                   Owner

Acquire current access token              Supabase auth helper

Attach Authorization header               authenticatedFetch / API client

Verify token                              NestJS AuthGuard

Parse non-2xx error envelope              API client

Cache successful response                 TanStack Query

Render state                              React component

