lessons.body:
Mutations and Targeted
Invalidation
Create and update remote state without manual refresh choreography

Phase 22 - TanStack Query
Volume 06 - Professional Frontend

Writes belong in mutations
export function useCreateTask() {
const queryClient = useQueryClient();

return useMutation({
mutationFn: createTask,
onSuccess: async () => {
await queryClient.invalidateQueries({
queryKey: taskKeys.lists(),
});
},
});
}

A successful create means cached Task lists may now be stale. We do not need to manually discover
every rendered list and call refetch on it. We invalidate the relevant key family.

Update mutation
export function useUpdateTask(taskId: string) {
const queryClient = useQueryClient();

return useMutation({
mutationFn: (input: UpdateTaskInput) => updateTask(taskId, input),
onSuccess: async (saved) => {
queryClient.setQueryData(taskKeys.detail(taskId), saved);
await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: taskKeys.lists() });
},
});
}

Why invalidate instead of patching every list manually?
TaskFlow lists can differ by status, priority, search, sort and page. A status update can move a record
out of one list and into another. Manual patching is possible, but it is easy to create subtle cache
inconsistencies. Phase 22 starts with targeted invalidation. Optimistic cache manipulation is
intentionally deferred to Phase 25.

Mutation retry
Mutations default to zero retries, which is safer for writes because a retry can repeat a side effect
unless the operation is known to be idempotent. TaskFlow keeps retry disabled until an operation
explicitly earns it.

Await invalidation when the UX depends on fresh data

If onSuccess returns the invalidateQueries promise, the mutation remains pending until the related active
queries have finished invalidation/refetch work. This can make “Save -> return to refreshed list” deterministic.

Invalidation matrix
Mutation                        Detail cache                         List caches

Create Task                     Usually no existing detail key       Invalidate Task lists

Update Task                     Set saved Task into its detail key   Invalidate lists because filters/sort
membership may change

Delete Task                     Remove or invalidate detail          Invalidate lists

Status transition               Refresh detail if viewed             Invalidate lists; record may enter or leave
filtered pages

This is deliberately conservative. Phase 25 can optimize perceived latency with optimistic updates after
rollback and concurrency hazards are understood.

