React Hook Form and Query
Mutations
Connect Phase 21 forms without merging unrelated state systems

Phase 22 - TanStack Query
Volume 06 - Professional Frontend

React Hook Form and TanStack Query have different
jobs
React Hook Form                                     TanStack Query

draft field values                               remote record cache

touched / dirty fields                            mutation pending state

field validation errors                             server request result

submit intent                                 related query invalidation

Phase 21 already built reliable field behavior. Phase 22 changes only the network side of submission.

const updateTaskMutation = useUpdateTask(taskId);

const onSubmit = handleSubmit(async (values) => {
clearErrors("root.server");
try {
const saved = await updateTaskMutation.mutateAsync(toApiInput(values));
reset(toFormValues(saved));
router.push("/tasks");
} catch (error) {
setError("root.server", {
type: "server",
message: getSafeMessage(error),
});
}
});

Which pending flag should disable Save?
React Hook Form has isSubmitting; TanStack mutation has isPending. If handleSubmit awaits
mutateAsync, isSubmitting naturally covers the submission promise. The mutation state remains useful
to other UI elements or extracted mutation components. Avoid inventing a third manual loading
boolean.

Server errors stay server errors
A 409 business conflict should not be rewritten as a fake client-side Zod field rule. Keep validation
responsibilities honest: Zod handles input shape; the server can reject valid-shaped data because of
current business state.

Form state is not cache state

Do not bind every keystroke directly into queryClient.setQueryData. Unsaved form edits belong to the form until
the server accepts them.

Submission sequence
User presses Save

React Hook Form validates client schema

mutateAsync sends accepted values

NestJS validates, authorizes and applies rules

Mutation resolves with saved Task

reset(saved values) + invalidate related queries

If any server step fails, the form retains the user's input. That is a better recovery experience than
clearing the form merely because an HTTP request was attempted.

